<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Library</OutputType>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;netstandard2.1;net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <PackageId>ClearBank.Net</PackageId>
    <AssemblyName>ClearBank.Net</AssemblyName>
    <Version>1.3.1</Version>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>v1.3.1:
- FIXED: a Target2 exchange rate is sent with its decimals (0.8571); 1.3.0 refused it and earlier versions rounded it to two
- FIXED: an amount carrying the float noise of a subtraction (10000000.01 - 10000000.0) is sent as 0.01; 1.3.0 refused it
- FIXED: a batch id, end-to-end id or sort code that is already percent-escaped (INV%2F1) is not escaped again
v1.3.0:
- BREAKING: UK webhook Payload.Reference, PaymentReference, TransactionCode and ServiceUserNumber are string option; Creditors[].Reference and SupplementaryData[].Name are string
- BREAKING: EU webhook Payload.Amount is decimal option; EndToEndIdentification and RemittanceInformation are string option
- FIXED: a call whose HttpClient followed a redirect is an Error (ClearBankRedirectException), not the redirect target's answer read as success
- FIXED: getEveryAccountAsync, getEveryTransactionAsync and getEveryAccountTransactionAsync return an Error for a page without its list, a null body or a repeated page
- FIXED: multi-currency cancelPaymentsAsync and the Bacs lists escape batch id, end-to-end id and sort code as path segments; an empty, "." or ".." value is an Error and nothing is sent
- FIXED: an account's minimum balance is sent as the decimal given on every target (.NET Framework sent -100.09999999999999 for -100.10)
- FIXED: the Bacs filter amount was formatted with the current culture
- CHANGED: a payment amount that two decimals don't hold (10.999, or too large for its pence) is an Error and nothing is sent; it was rounded (FPS, CHAPS, multi-currency, SEPA, Target2)
- ADDED: ClearBankRedirectException with the URI sent and the URI that answered
v1.2.0:
- FIXED: the token reaches the HTTP call of every UK v1 and v2 operation, so cancelling stops it
- FIXED: cancelling a configuration-based call ends Canceled with OperationCanceledException, not Faulted; a timeout stays an Error
- FIXED: printing ClearbankConfiguration or ClearBankClient (%A, ToString) hides the API token
- FIXED: a webhook nonce above the Int32 range no longer overflows the response or the EU parse
- BREAKING: WebHookResponse.Nonce and the EU webhook's Nonce are int64
v1.1.2:
- ADDED: Api.getEveryAccountAsync, getEveryTransactionAsync and getEveryAccountTransactionAsync read every page
v1.1.1:
- FIXED: the HttpClients made here no longer follow redirects, which sent signatures and payment bodies to the redirect's host; a 3xx answer is an error
v1.1.0:
- BREAKING: SwaggerProvider 4.2.1: generated models take and return option for optional strings, Guid for ids, DateTimeOffset for date-times; multi-currency AccountIdentifier kind is an enum
- CHANGED: FSharp.Core 10.1.401, FSharp.Data 8.2.0, KeyVaultSigning 1.0.13 (async signing-client cache fix)
- CHANGED: legacy DateTime filters of unspecified kind are sent as UTC
- FIXED: bundled v1/v2 schemas: response keys with spaces, a non-map examples and query uniqueItems that the OpenAPI reader rejects
- ADDED: CHAPS v6 customer, institution and return payments (chapsCustomerPaymentAsync, chapsInstitutionPaymentAsync, chapsReturnPaymentAsync, chapsAccount)
- ADDED: interest-bearing account closure: requestAccountClosureAsync, getAccountClosureAsync
- ADDED: bundled sterling-v1, cop-outbound-v1, cop-accounts-v1 and chaps-v6 schemas; chaps-v6 amount as double
- FIXED: payment amounts were formatted with the current culture: under a decimal-comma culture (fi-FI, de-DE) every FPS, SEPA, T2, multi-currency and CHAPS payment failed
- FIXED: a request that cannot be serialized is an Error, not an exception
- FIXED: multi-currency payment amounts were float32 (1234567.89 was sent as 1234567.9); PaymentRequestItem amount is now float, sent with two decimals
- ADDED: RequestSigner: Azure Key Vault, local RSA key, or a SHA-256 digest delegate (AWS KMS) for DigitalSignature
- ADDED: ClearBankClient over a caller-owned, shared HttpClient; Task-based UK.Api, UK.MultiCurrency.Api and EU.Api with CancellationToken
- ADDED: UK accounts: get by id, update (status, reason, owner, minimum balance), close
- ADDED: UK virtual accounts: create, list, list all, get, update, disable
- ADDED: Bacs Direct Debit mandates: list, cancel, return, collections, unpaid collections; transaction returns; unpaid Direct Debits and unapplied Direct Credits
- ADDED: per-account and per-virtual-account transactions
- ADDED: Confirmation of Payee name verification, Secondary Reference Data check, inbound CoP opt-out
- ADDED: multi-currency payment cancellation
- ADDED: typed UkWebhook / EuWebhook with webhookTypeUK / webhookTypeEU; createSignedResponseAsync with any signer
- ADDED: ClearBankResponseException carries the status and body of non-success responses
- FIXED: multi-currency updateAccount, updateAccountStatus and addCurrency sent Authorization, DigitalSignature and X-Request-Id in the wrong headers
- FIXED: multi-currency deleteAccount sent no Authorization header
- CHANGED: the configuration-based functions delegate to the Task API and create their HttpClient when run, not when called</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <TargetFSharpCoreVersion>8.0.0.0</TargetFSharpCoreVersion>
    <Authors>Tuomas, Simon</Authors>
    <Company>Fund Ourselves</Company>
    <PackageTags>ClearBank .NET client clear bank integration payments online payment library transaction api bank uk automation england united-kingdom great-britain eu gbp eur hsm banking gateway clearbank</PackageTags>
    <Description>
        Unofficial .NET client for ClearBank integration, creating online payments via their API.
        Bank payment handling automation in United Kingdom and EU.
    </Description>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Thorium/ClearBank.Net.git</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>Unlicense</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <IsTestProject>false</IsTestProject>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <AllowedOutputExtensionsInPackageBuildOutputFolder>$(AllowedOutputExtensionsInPackageBuildOutputFolder);.pdb</AllowedOutputExtensionsInPackageBuildOutputFolder>
    <PackageReadmeFile>Readme.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="ClearBankTests" />
    <None Include="Readme.md" Link="Readme.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <Compile Include="ClearBank.Common.fs" />
    <Compile Include="ClearBank.UK.fs" />
    <Compile Include="ClearBank.EU.fs" />
    <Compile Include="WebhookParsing.fs" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="FSharp.Data" Version="8.2.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="FSharp.Data.JsonProvider.Serializer" Version="1.0.8" />
    <PackageReference Include="KeyVaultSigning" Version="1.0.13" />
    <PackageReference Include="Newtonsoft.Json" Version="13.0.3" />
    <PackageReference Include="SwaggerProvider" Version="4.2.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Diagnostics.DiagnosticSource" Version="9.0.4" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Update="FSharp.Core" Version="10.1.401" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
